est harness pass ?tour=0. Dock the panel so it never sits over .hive-panels: position:fixed; right:12px; bottom:12px; max-width:280px. On phone (max-width:720px) make it a bottom sheet whose height is reserved with padding-bottom on .hive-shell.\n2. PROBLEM: The project name in each node header is dark text on the control-yellow header and is almost unreadable. The body shows 'asks / out / fails' with every value as '—' and no p() meter row, so the cards carry no usable data.\n   WHERE: All five node cards (project-swarm, agent-data-business, swarm-practice, parts-request-app, blackbook-app)\n   FILE: tools/watch-assets/cc-hive.css + tools/watch-assets/cc-hive-mount.js\n   CHANGE: Set .hive-node-hd { color:#0a0a0c; font-weight:700; font-size:11px } and remove any opacity or faint colour on the name span. Map real per-project board fields into the kv rows, e.g. asks = needs-you count, out = open/done tickets, fails = failed jobs. Render a real 0 rather than '—' when the field exists and is zero. Add the .hive-meter row (track + .fill width from done/total tickets) as in the mockup. Give dt/dd line-height:1.35 so the three rows don't crowd together.\n3. PROBLEM: The stage is top-heavy. All cards sit in slots 0-2 at the top, the bottom ~40% of the stage is empty, and three particle streams leave the right of the ring pointing at nothing.\n   WHERE: Hive stage, centre/right of the ring (around x 830-870, y 450-510) and the empty band at y 500-700\n   FILE: tools/watch-assets/cc-hive-mount.js\n   CHANGE: Spread the slots over the real node count per side: slotTop = i * (100 / max(nodesOnSide,1)) with height capped at min(CARD_HEIGHT_PCT, 100/nodesOnSide - gap), and centre the column vertically (offset = (100 - used)/2). Build streams only for nodes that have a laid-out box (skip entries where box is null or width is 0) so no orphan streams are drawn.\n4. PROBLEM: The 'ANSWER BEFORE YOU SPEND' label renders as flat text above the ring instead of on the orbit arc. On phone