panel{overflow:visible;min-height:auto}. Remove the empty placeholder box when there are no samples.\n6. PROBLEM: There is no prioritised 'needs you / failed / next' list. The owner has to scan the cards to find the 6 asks, and the debug-ish caption 'Live board data from your Swarm watch server.' takes prime space.\n   WHERE: Header caption under the logo; no attention list exists\n   FILE: tools/watch-assets/hive-panels.js, cc-hive.css\n   CHANGE: Replace the caption with a compact 'Needs you' list (project bot, ask title, age, status pill, an 'Open' pill button that links to that project's Cockpit), sorted with failed first, then asks, then next. Place it as the first bottom panel, or as a right rail on desktop and directly under the stats on phone.\n\nSCREENSHOTS: open and LOOK at coordination/review/cc-grade/r4/now-hive-desktop.png and coordination/review/cc-grade/r4/now-hive-phone.png before you change anything: they are the current render of this code on a populated board (1440x900 and 390x844). The hive-desktop.png and hive-phone.png files in the same folder are what the grader saw. After each fix, re-read your CSS and markup and check it against what you saw; you cannot re-render, so reason concretely about sizes (card heights vs content, grid tracks, overflow, fixed heights at 390px).\nCard values: bind asks to the needs-you field, out to card.out (agents.jobs.running), fails to card.fails, meter from card.meter (tools/command-center-snapshot.mjs, read-only); lane colour per card from the project lane the snapshot computes; the hub ring state must reflect live agents (not resting when agents are running).",
