ls match. Rename 'projects running' to 'projects active', or count only the running state. Render log times as relative time from each event's own timestamp (e.g. '12s', '3m') rather than the render time.\n4. PROBLEM: Projects use plain letter avatars (P / A / S / B) instead of the colourful robot-head assets. The page also has no visible glitch accent, so two of the owner's stated taste items are missing.\n   WHERE: Project cards on the hub map and the avatars in the Needs You rows\n   FILE: tools/watch-assets/hive-panels.js\n   CHANGE: Swap the letter tile for the robot-head asset, picked deterministically by a hash of the project id: <img class=\"cc-avatar\" src=\"robot-heads/${idx}.svg\" alt=\"\">. Add a single glitch effect to the 'opus' hub wordmark only: .cc-hub-title { position: relative } .cc-hub-title::before,::after { content: attr(data-text); clip-path: inset(..); animation: cc-glitch 6s steps(1) infinite; }, disabled under prefers-reduced-motion and the Pause motion toggle.\n5. PROBLEM: The spend value reads '$41.8' (dropping the trailing zero looks like a bug). The FAILS tiles show '—' on every project, which says nothing about whether anything failed.\n   WHERE: SPEND stat card, Throughput 'board spend' row, and the FAILS tile in each project card\n   FILE: tools/watch-assets/hive-panels.js\n   CHANGE: Format currency with Intl.NumberFormat('en-US',{style:'currency',currency:'USD',minimumFractionDigits:2}). Show a muted '0' in FAILS when the count is known to be zero, keep '—' only when there is no data, and colour FAILS > 0 red with a pill.\n6. PROBLEM: On phone the header controls wrap into an uneven row of five pills, and the LIVE chip loses its agent count. The hub map cards below repeat what Needs You and the stat cards already show.\n   WHERE: Phone header (y 40-85) and the hub map section below Needs You\n   FILE: tools/watch-assets/cc-hive.css\n   CHANGE: @media (max-width:480px){ .cc-hive-nav { display:grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3,1fr) auto auto; gap:6px } .cc-live-chip .count { display:inline } }. Collapse the hub map into a compact 2-col grid of project tiles with min-height:44px tap targets.\n\nSCREENSHOTS: open and LOOK at coordination/review/cc-grade/r5/hive-desktop.png (1440x900) and coordination/review/cc-grade/r5/hive-phone.png (390x844) before changing anything; they are this code rendered on a populated board. You cannot re-render, so reason concretely about sizes (heights vs content, grid tracks, overflow, fixed heights at 390px).\nGLITCH: exactly one glitch effect for the whole app: the brand wordmark (jev + opus) on both pages, short and on load/hover only, using tools/watch-assets/cc-glitch.js; respect prefers-reduced-motion. Nothing else glitches.\nROBOT HEADS: replace the letter avatars on project cards and in the Needs You list with the colourful robot-head assets already in tools/watch-assets (robot-avatar.js, robot-head.js, robot-color.js and friends; read them and reuse their API; colour derived from the project id so it is stable). Do not redraw robots.\nYou also own the brand glitch for both pages via the shared header code your files render; if the Cockpit header is built only in Cockpit files, implement the glitch helper usage in your files and say in your summary how Cockpit should call it.",
