electorAll results; use Array.from (tests/watch-assets-dom-collections.test.mjs enforces it).\nExactly one tasteful glitch effect in the whole app (the brand wordmark, via tools/watch-assets/cc-glitch.js, read-only). Read coordination/review/cc-design-contract.md for file ownership; if an item needs a file outside your outputs, skip it and name it in your summary.\nYou also own the first-visit tour (tools/watch-assets/cc-tour.js) for both pages: it never opens by itself; only the help button starts it.\n\nGRADER ITEMS:\n1. PROBLEM: Project nodes are stacked in two straight columns (5 left, 4 right) instead of being placed AROUND the ring at even angles like the target's clock-face layout (top, upper-left/right, sides, lower-left/right, bottom).\n   WHERE: Main stage, both node columns\n   FILE: tools/watch-assets/cc-hive-mount.js, tools/watch-assets/cc-hive.css\n   CHANGE: Drop the two flex columns; make the stage position:relative with a fixed aspect, and absolutely position each node at angle a_i = -90deg + i(any)360/n on an ellipse (left: calc(50% + rx(any)cos(a)), top: calc(50% + ry(any)sin(a)), transform: translate(-50%,-50%)), with rx about 40% and ry about 38% of the stage so the nodes ring the core.\n2. PROBLEM: The ring is small (about 220px) and plain: a dashed maroon band with a teal outline. The target's ring is huge (about 45% of the stage width) and glows pink/magenta, with a violet inner circle around the OPUS core and faint radial spokes.\n   WHERE: Centre of stage\n   FILE: tools/watch-assets/cc-hive.css\n   CHANGE: Size the ring with width: min(46vw, 560px); aspect-ratio: 1. Give it border: 3px solid #ff3d7f; box-shadow: 0 0 24px #ff3d7f, 0 0 80px rgba(255,61,127,.55), inset 0 0 60px rgba(255,61,127,.35). Add an inner .core circle about 40% of the ring with a 1.5px #8b6cff border and a violet glow, plus a repeating-conic-gradient layer for thin radial spokes at 0.08 opacity.\n3. PROBLEM: Each node feeds the ring through a single thin yellow dotted 