 CHANGE: Render .row as a grid (chip | title/sub | check/tag). Fill the chip with var(--cat-color), pick the colour from the ticket's lane/category, and put the category name in 9px letter-spaced caps at the bottom right. Keep status as a check (done), a pulsing dot (running) or nothing (ready). Add a translateX offset per row (left column: indent that grows then shrinks; right column: mirrored) to recreate the target's bowed arc. Use a 1.5px border coloured by category at 0.5 alpha.\n3. PROBLEM: There is no centred title box. The target has a boxed 'OPUS 5.5' title with a small orange subline above the robot; here there is only a small 'thinking' chip.\n   WHERE: Top of the centre column\n   FILE: tools/watch-assets/cockpit-view.js, tools/watch-assets/cc-cockpit.css\n   CHANGE: Add a .title-box above the robot: a 1.5px orange border, 4px radius, the model/orchestrator name in 28px letter-spaced mono caps, and a 9px orange caps subline built from the live lane names. Keep the 'thinking' state as a small chip inside or under it.\n4. PROBLEM: The robot and its orbit don't match: a space-invader sprite with a thin white ellipse cutting through it, no warm radial glow and floor shadow, and no dotted path running from the robot to the active row.\n   WHERE: Centre column, robot\n   FILE: tools/watch-assets/cockpit-view.js, tools/watch-assets/cc-cockpit.css\n   CHANGE: Draw the target's block-creature silhouette (wide head, two black square eyes, side arms, four legs) as a CSS grid of #e07a5f cells, about 300px wide. Add a radial-gradient(circle, rgba(224,122,95,.25), transparent 60%) glow behind it and a dark ellipse floor shadow. Render the orbit as a tilted SVG ellipse (stroke rgba(255,255,255,.25)) behind the body. Add an SVG path with stroke-dasharray '1 6' and round caps from the orbit edge to the active row's chip, with node dots, recomputed on resize and on active-row change.\n5. PROBLEM: The segmented multi-colour rule is a single orange bar plus a separate availability bar. The target uses short dashes coloured per lane, with the lane names above and 'LIVE SCAN / n OF m' on the right.\n   WHERE: Under the subhead\n   FILE: tools/watch-assets/cockpit-view.js, tools/watch-assets/cc-cockpit.css\n   CHANGE: Replace both bars with one .seg-rule using display: flex; gap: 6px. Render one 3px segment per ticket, coloured by its lane (dimmed to 0.3 alpha when not done), and put a 'LIVE SCAN / done OF total' mono label at the right end in orange/pink.\n6. PROBLEM: Almost nothing moves between frames; the only change is a faint dimming of the RUNNING chips. The target implies a scanning active row, an advancing orbit and dotted path, and filling progress bars.\n   WHERE: Whole page\n   FILE: tools/watch-assets/cc-cockpit.css\n   CHANGE: Add @keyframes for: a dot travelling the orbit ellipse (offset-path, 6s linear infinite); a dash march on the dotted path (stroke-dashoffset, 1.2s linear infinite); a scanline sweep across the active row (linear-gradient background-position, 2.4s); a 2-frame robot leg bob (steps(2), 0.8s); and a subtle shimmer on progress bar fills. Respect prefers-reduced-motion and the pause toggle.\n7. PROBLEM: The 'how the loop works' strip is a collapsed disclosure. The target shows an always-visible loop strip with an orange caps label and a '>'-separated sequence of steps, with the last step in orange.\n   WHERE: Below the ticket grid\n   FILE: tools/watch-assets/cockpit-view.js, tools/watch-assets/cc-cockpit.css\n   CHANGE: Render .loop-strip as an open bordered band: an orange 10px caps label on the left, a right-aligned caps note, and a row of 12px mono step labels separated by muted '>' glyphs, with the currently active stage highlighted in orange.\n8. PROBLEM: The run stream card shows the run id twice ('17933130 17933130'), and the big empty area under the left ticket column wastes space.\n   WHERE: Centre run-stream card; lower-left grid\n   FILE: tools/watch-assets/cockpit-view.js, tools/watch-assets/cockpit-lists.js\n   CHANGE: Show the run id once, followed by the run's label/stage from the board. Balance the columns by splitting tickets ceil(n/2) per side (or up to 10 per column, as in the target) and let the grid height follow its content (align-items: start) so no empty panel remains.",
