+   "prompt": "S10 Command Center, Hive page, round 7 (Hive scored 3.6/5 against the target; goal 4.5+).\nGOAL: the owner wants this page to look IDENTICAL to the target image docs/design/reference/hive-target.png in composition, components, styling and motion. OPEN AND STUDY THE TARGET IMAGE FIRST, then the current screenshots: coordination/review/cc-grade/r7/hive-desktop.png (1440x900), coordination/review/cc-grade/r7/hive-desktop-b.png (same page about 0.8 s later: if the two look the same, nothing is animating) and coordination/review/cc-grade/r7/hive-phone.png (390x844; the target has no phone view, so make a faithful single-column adaptation), and coordination/review/cc-grade/r7/hive-full.png (the whole desktop page including what is below the fold).\nThe target's text and numbers are illustrative. Keep the app's REAL data (project names, ticket titles, counts) and its data bindings; match everything else: layout and placement, shapes, borders, glows, gradients, colours, typography, spacing, icons, and animations.\nMotion is required where the target implies it (particles and streams flowing, the ring and orbit, scan or progress motion, live chips pulsing), with CSS animations or requestAnimationFrame on canvas/SVG, smooth at 60 fps, paused under prefers-reduced-motion.\nFix every grader item below in order, then keep going toward the target until you run out of clear differences. You cannot re-render, so reason concretely about sizes at 1440x900 and 390x844 (heights vs content, grid tracks, overflow).\nNever hard-code sample numbers. Empty values render as a short muted line, never a blank box.\nKeep every hook other code and tests rely on: #command-center-root, .hive-shell, [data-project-id] on Hive project nodes, .cc-cockpit-shell, #cc-cockpit-main, and the stylesheet links in command-center.html (you cannot edit that file). Existing tests in your context must keep passing; update a test only where it asserted the old look, never its data behaviour.\nReal browsers: never call array methods on .children/.childNodes/getElementsByTagName/getElementsByClassName/querySelectorAll results; use Array.from (tests/watch-assets-dom-collections.test.mjs enforces it).\nExactly one tasteful glitch effect in the whole app (the brand wordmark, via tools/watch-assets/cc-glitch.js, read-only). Read coordination/review/cc-design-contract.md for file ownership; if an item needs a file outside your outputs, skip it and name it in your summary.\nYou also own the first-visit tour (tools/watch-assets/cc-tour.js) for both pages: it never opens by itself; only the help button starts it.\n\nGRADER ITEMS:\n1. PROBLEM: The composition is taller than the target. The bottom nodes (06, 05) are cut off at the 900px fold, and the lane legend, italic tagline and all three bottom panels sit off-screen. In the target, the whole ring plus all nodes fit above the legend row.\n   WHERE: Whole Hive stage, below the ring\n   FILE: tools/watch-assets/cc-hive.css\n   CHANGE: Size the stage from the viewport, e.g. .cc-hive-stage{height:min(78vh,720px)}. Shrink the ring to about 46% of the stage height and place the nodes on an ellipse radius tied to it, so nodes 05/06 end above about 760px and the legend/tagline row shows at the bottom of the first screen.\n2. PROBLEM: The particle streams from nodes into the ring are thin single lines with a few sparks. The target has dense, lane-coloured particle sprays fanning out from each node and converging on the ring.\n   WHERE: Between each node card and the ring\n   FILE: tools/watch-assets/cc-hive-mount.js\n   CHANGE: Per node, emit 30-60 particles in the node's lane colour along a bezier from the card edge to the ring, with ±12px perpendicular jitter, size 1-3px and additive blending (globalCompositeOperation='lighter'). Add a soft radial bloom where each stream meets the ring.\n3. PROBLEM: The extra nav row (The Hive / Command Center / Cockpit / Classic / Search / Tour) and the 'A run failed' toast are not in the target. They push the composition down, and the toast covers the area near node 02.\n   WHERE: Below the header rule, top right\n   FILE: tools/watch-assets/cc-hive.css\n   CHANGE: Fold the nav into the header as small mono links next to LIVE (font-size 11px, letter-spacing .2em) or into a hover overflow. Move the toast to bottom-right of the viewport, above the footer, with position:fixed; bottom:24px.\n4. PROBLEM: The node card headers use a status label (NEEDS YOU/BUILDING/IDLE) plus an emoji robot and badge icons. The target shows a clean index + name + lane tag. Names are truncated with an ellipsis (forge-recipe-ca…, parts-request-…).\n   WHERE: Node card header bars\n   FILE: tools/watch-assets/hive-panels.js\n   CHANGE: Render the header as `NN name` + a right-aligned lane tag in 9px mono caps. Move the needs-you count into a small pill inside the card body. Raise the card min-width to 260px and reduce the name font size to 12px before truncating.\n5. PROBLEM: The footer row duplicates the percentage: a coloured '71%' on the left and '.71' on the right. The target has one label like p(x) on the left and one value on the right.\n   WHERE: Node card bottom progress row\n   FILE: tools/watch-assets/hive-panels.js\n   CHANGE: Replace the left percent with a mono label such as `p(done)` in the lane colour and keep the right `.71` value, matching the target's p(label) / bar / value layout.\n6. PROBLEM: The ring's core glow is weaker than the target. The target ring is a saturated pink-to-violet gradient with heavy outer bloom; here the inner rings read grey and busy with coloured dashes.\n   WHERE: Central ring\n   FILE: tools/watch-assets/cc-hive.css\n   CHANGE: Give the main ring a conic-gradient stroke (#ff3d8b→#c86bff→#ff3d8b) with filter: drop-shadow(0 0 18px #ff3d8bcc) drop-shadow(0 0 48px #b04dff66). Make the inner tick ring 30% opacity and drop the multi-coloured dash confetti inside it.\n7. PROBLEM: The ring label letters are spaced unevenly and are the same weight as the surroundings. In the target the label sits tight along the arc in small spaced mono.\n   WHERE: Arc text around the ring\n   FILE: tools/watch-assets/cc-hive-mount.js\n   CHANGE: Use an SVG <textPath> on a circle 14px outside the ring with font-size 11px, letter-spacing 0.45em and fill rgba(255,255,255,.75), and animate startOffset slowly (60s linear infinite).\n8. PROBLEM: Phone: the 'A run failed' toast overlaps the first node card, and the nav tabs wrap onto two lines above the ring.\n   WHERE: Hive phone, bottom of first screen\n   FILE: tools/watch-assets/cc-hive.css\n   CHANGE: At max-width:480px, make the nav a single horizontally scrollable row (overflow-x:auto; white-space:nowrap). Give the toast bottom:calc(env(safe-area-inset-bottom)+12px) and pad the content below it so the toast never covers a card.\n\nCOORDINATOR NOTES: the 900px first screen should match the target composition: drop the extra nav row (keep a compact nav in the header line as the target does), never show a toast over the stage (move notifications into the header LIVE area), and fit the ring and all node cards above the fold at 1440x900 with the legend/tagline row just below.",
