ta behaviour.\nReal browsers: never call array methods on .children/.childNodes/getElementsByTagName/getElementsByClassName/querySelectorAll results; use Array.from (tests/watch-assets-dom-collections.test.mjs enforces it).\nExactly one tasteful glitch effect in the whole app (the brand wordmark, via tools/watch-assets/cc-glitch.js, read-only). Read coordination/review/cc-design-contract.md for file ownership; if an item needs a file outside your outputs, skip it and name it in your summary.\nThe tour (cc-tour.js) belongs to the parallel Hive job; do not edit it. The big pixel robot may reuse tools/watch-assets/robot-head.js (read-only) if it can match the target's flat orange pixel creature; otherwise draw it in your own files.\n\nGRADER ITEMS:\n1. PROBLEM: The central figure is a glossy 3D purple box robot. The target is a flat, large pixel-art creature in one warm colour, with blocky square eyes and legs and a flat shadow ellipse.\n   WHERE: Centre of the Cockpit stage\n   FILE: tools/watch-assets/cockpit-view.js\n   CHANGE: Render the robot as an SVG/CSS grid of square pixels (e.g. 12x10 cells, 28px each, shape-rendering:crispEdges) in one accent fill, with two dark square eyes and four leg columns. Add a flat dark ellipse shadow underneath and no gradients or 3D shading.\n2. PROBLEM: The segmented multi-colour rule under the headline is a single solid green line. The target is a row of short separated segments coloured by category.\n   WHERE: Rule under the subhead, y≈190\n   FILE: tools/watch-assets/cc-cockpit.css\n   CHANGE: Render one segment per ticket (or per category share) as a flex row with gap:6px. Each segment is height:3px with background:var(--cat-color) from its category, and done segments get full opacity, the rest .35.\n3. PROBLEM: The index chips are all the same cyan, and the right tag shows status (RUNNING/READY/DONE) rather than a coloured category tag. The target colour-codes the chip, left border and tag by category.\n   WHERE: Both ticket columns\n   FILE: tools/watch-assets/cockpit-lists.js\n   CHANGE: Derive a category per ticket from real board data (lane/area/type). Set --cat-color on the row and use it for the chip background, the left border and the tag text. Show status as the check/play glyph only.\n4. PROBLEM: The dotted path goes to the right-column DONE row (photo upload retries), while NOW RUNNING names T-0615 in the left column. The path should point at the active row.\n   WHERE: Path from the orbit ellipse to the right column\n   FILE: tools/watch-assets/cockpit-view.js\n   CHANGE: Compute the path target from the same active ticket as the NOW RUNNING card, and give that row the highlighted border state. If the active row is in the left column, draw the path to that side.\n5. PROBLEM: Almost nothing changes between the two frames: only the orbit dots move and the robot's mouth pixels change. The target feels live, with a scanning highlight, a pulsing active row and filling progress.\n   WHERE: Whole stage\n   FILE: tools/watch-assets/cc-cockpit.css\n   CHANGE: Add @keyframes for (a) a dash-offset march on the dotted path (stroke-dasharray:2 6; animation: dash 1.2s linear infinite), (b) a soft border pulse on the active row, and (c) a 3-4s scan sweep across the segmented rule, plus a gentle 2px idle bob on the robot.\n6. PROBLEM: The breadcrumb is merged into a stat/nav bar with pills (THE HIVE, Command Center, Classic). The target has a plain small mono breadcrumb on the left and a meta line on the right.\n   WHERE: Top line\n   FILE: tools/watch-assets/cockpit-view.js\n   CHANGE: Render the top line as `SW / THE HIVE / PARTS-REQUEST-APP` in 11px bold mono caps with letter-spacing .12em, and put `N TICKETS / AGENTS / DATE` right-aligned in the same style. Move the view switch into a small overflow.\n7. PROBLEM: The NOW RUNNING card is narrower than and offset from the target's NOW LOADING card. The title box 'ORCHESTRATOR' is fine, but the card lacks the target's big title weight and the orange 'GETS >' line.\n   WHERE: Card under the robot\n   FILE: tools/watch-assets/cc-cockpit.css\n   CHANGE: Align the card width to the title box column (same left/right edges). Set the title to font-size 26px, weight 800, and render the last line as `WORKER > …` with the label in the accent orange (#ff7a45) and 10px mono caps.\n8. PROBLEM: Phone: the robot fills most of the screen and pushes NOW RUNNING below the fold. The header wordmark is clipped to 'SWA', and the meta line is truncated ('S19 …').\n   WHERE: Cockpit phone\n   FILE: tools/watch-assets/cc-cockpit.css\n   CHANGE: At max-width:480px, cap the robot at max-height:200px, show the full short wordmark 'SW' (or let it wrap), and let the meta line wrap with white-space:normal so the NOW RUNNING card shows near the first screen.\n\nCOORDINATOR NOTES: (a) The centre figure must be the target's FLAT pixel-art creature (one warm orange colour, blocky square eyes, four legs, flat shadow ellipse beneath, orbit ellipse around it), drawn on canvas in tools/watch-assets/cc-cockpit-orbit.js, not the 3D robot head; it can still show state by small eye changes. (b) Category = the ticket's lane or type from the ledger (whichever is present); give each category a fixed colour and use it for the index chip, the left border, the right tag and the segmented rule under the headline. (c) The dotted path must end at the row of the NOW RUNNING ticket.",
