rowsers: never call array methods on .children/.childNodes/getElementsByTagName/getElementsByClassName/querySelectorAll results; use Array.from (tests/watch-assets-dom-collections.test.mjs enforces it).\nExactly one tasteful glitch effect in the whole app (the brand wordmark, via tools/watch-assets/cc-glitch.js, read-only). Read coordination/review/cc-design-contract.md for file ownership; if an item needs a file outside your outputs, skip it and name it in your summary.\nYou also own the first-visit tour (tools/watch-assets/cc-tour.js) for both pages: it never opens by itself; only the help button starts it.\n\nGRADER ITEMS:\n1. PROBLEM: Particle streams are far too faint and sparse. The target has dense, bright lane-coloured sprays bursting from every node into the ring; the app shows a few dim dots and thin curved lines, so the ring looks disconnected from the nodes.\n   WHERE: Between each project card and the ring, all around the centre\n   FILE: tools/watch-assets/cc-hive-mount.js\n   CHANGE: Raise the per-node particle budget to roughly 60-120, draw with ctx.globalCompositeOperation='lighter', radius 1-2.5px with shadowBlur 6-10px in the lane colour, emit along a bezier from the card edge to the ring with a bright comet head and a tapering trail, and add a few 3-4px bloomed sparks per stream.\n2. PROBLEM: The ring is smaller, thinner and less layered than the target's. The target ring is a thick glowing band with two inner concentric rings, a dotted outer ring, radial spokes and a heavy pink bloom; the app ring is a single thin gradient stroke with a modest glow.\n   WHERE: Centre of the page\n   FILE: tools/watch-assets/cc-hive.css\n   CHANGE: Scale the ring to about 30% of viewport width (the target is ~440px at 1320px), make the main band 6-8px, add two thinner inner rings and a 1px dotted outer ring, stack glows (filter: drop-shadow(0 0 24px) and drop-shadow(0 0 60px) in pink/violet), and draw the radial spokes at ~0.15 opacity.\n3. PROBLEM: The session log has no mini bar chart. The target ends the log with the command line and a coloured 'forks per second' bar chart; the app shows the command line then the note 'no completion times in the ledger' and a large empty area.\n   WHERE: Bottom-left panel, below the command line\n   FILE: tools/watch-assets/hive-panels.js\n   CHANGE: Derive the chart from data that is present (session-log events per minute, or tickets per project coloured by status), render ~40 bars 4px wide in lane colours with a mono caption, and only show the text note when there are literally zero events.\n4. PROBLEM: The right panel has no step chart. The target shows four bars, then a pink glowing step-line ('decision latency'), then two stat rows; the app has the bars and stat rows with nothing in between and empty space below.\n   WHERE: Bottom-right panel, below the four status bars\n   FILE: tools/watch-assets/hive-panels.js\n   CHANGE: Render an SVG step-line (stroke pink 1.5px, filter drop-shadow glow) from a real series such as cumulative done counts or done-per-project percentages, with a small mono caption beneath, and keep the stat rows under it so the panel ends level with the others.\n5. PROBLEM: The 'who answered' bars are missing. The target's middle panel shows three coloured bars with right-aligned values; the app's 'WHO BUILT (24 H)' section shows the note 'no per-lane job counts in the board data' instead.\n   WHERE: Middle panel, below DONE PER PROJECT\n   FILE: tools/watch-assets/hive-panels.js\n   CHANGE: Compute the bars from a grouping that is available (tickets by worker kind, or done / in review / ready) with coloured bar fills and values in the matching colour; show the note only when no grouping exists.\n6. PROBLEM: The three bottom panels are uneven. The extra nine-row DONE PER PROJECT list makes the middle panel ~700px tall while the left and right columns have large empty areas; in the target all three columns are equally dense and end on one line.\n   WHERE: Bottom panel block\n   FILE: tools/watch-assets/hive-panels.js\n   CHANGE: Render done-per-project as a compact two-column mini list (or top N with '+n more'), move the stat rows up, and set the grid to align-items: stretch with content padding so all three columns finish at the same height.\n7. PROBLEM: The header carries an extra navigation row (COMMAND CENTER / COCKPIT / CLASSIC / SEARCH / TOUR) under the counters, and the 'A run failed' toast is jammed against the header rule beside it. The target header is only wordmark, description, counters and LIVE.\n   WHERE: Header, right side\n   FILE: tools/watch-assets/cc-hive.css\n   CHANGE: Collapse the nav into a small '···' menu at the far right of the counters (or move it to the footer line), and position the toast fixed at bottom-right with a slide-in animation so it never touches the header.\n8. PROBLEM: On the phone the nav row overflows and is clipped on the left ('ENTER' is all that remains of COMMAND CENTER), hiding content.\n   WHERE: Phone view, below LIVE\n   FILE: tools/watch-assets/cc-hive.css\n   CHANGE: In the max-width: 480px rule set the nav to flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: flex-start; overflow: visible with a 6px row gap, or hide it behind the same '···' menu.\n\nCOORDINATOR NOTES: the floating help button and the extra nav row are yours (cc-tour.js and the header in cc-hive-mount.js): put the nav into the single header line like the target (small mono links), make help a small header link, and move the run-failed notice into the header LIVE area. For the who-answered bars and the charts, use the snapshot fields the port added in tools/command-center-snapshot.mjs (read-only here); if a field is missing, show the chart with a muted note instead of dropping it.",
