ta behaviour.\nReal browsers: never call array methods on .children/.childNodes/getElementsByTagName/getElementsByClassName/querySelectorAll results; use Array.from (tests/watch-assets-dom-collections.test.mjs enforces it).\nExactly one tasteful glitch effect in the whole app (the brand wordmark, via tools/watch-assets/cc-glitch.js, read-only). Read coordination/review/cc-design-contract.md for file ownership; if an item needs a file outside your outputs, skip it and name it in your summary.\nThe tour (cc-tour.js) belongs to the parallel Hive job; do not edit it. The big pixel robot may reuse tools/watch-assets/robot-head.js (read-only) if it can match the target's flat orange pixel creature; otherwise draw it in your own files.\n\nGRADER ITEMS:\n1. PROBLEM: The two columns are unbalanced. The target has two full columns of ten rows numbered 01-20 continuously; the app shows eight rows on the left and only three on the right (numbered 01-03 again), leaving a large empty area under the right column down to the loop strip.\n   WHERE: Right ticket column\n   FILE: tools/watch-assets/cockpit-lists.js\n   CHANGE: Build one ordered list of every ticket in the stage (running, then ready, then done), split it in half across the two columns with continuous numbering, use the ON chip for running, the play glyph for ready and the check for done; and give the column container align-content: space-between so a shorter column still spans the height.\n2. PROBLEM: Counts contradict each other: the header says 5 DONE and 9 LEFT, the right column shows three done rows, the left column eight open rows, and the worker stream shows four finished tickets.\n   WHERE: Header stats, ticket columns, worker stream\n   FILE: tools/watch-assets/cockpit-lists.js\n   CHANGE: Drive the header counts, both columns and the stream from the same ticket array with no per-column cap or stage filter, and if a column must be truncated append a '+n more' row so the visible numbers still add up.\n3. PROBLEM: Almost nothing moves between frames: only the orbit dot and the path pulse shift. The robot, its glow, the ON chip, the LIVE dot and the stream progress bars are static.\n   WHERE: Centre robot, active row, stream cards\n   FILE: tools/watch-assets/cc-cockpit.css\n   CHANGE: Add a 4s ease-in-out translateY(-6px) bob on the robot with the shadow ellipse scaling inversely, a slow stroke-dashoffset drift on the orbit ellipse, an opacity pulse on the ON chip and LIVE dot, and animate stream progress bars from 0 to their width on mount.\n4. PROBLEM: A floating '?' help button overlaps the SWARM LOOP strip on desktop and sits on top of the 03 index chip on the phone; the target has no floating controls.\n   WHERE: Bottom-left of the viewport\n   FILE: tools/watch-assets/cc-cockpit.css\n   CHANGE: Move the help control into the breadcrumb bar beside the '···' button, or make it position: fixed; right: 16px; bottom: 16px with a high z-index and a 12px safe margin so it never covers content.\n5. PROBLEM: The dotted path from the orbit to the active row is a jagged polyline with large white dots; the target uses a smooth curve with small dots and a bright node at each end.\n   WHERE: Between the orbit ellipse and the active row\n   FILE: tools/watch-assets/cockpit-view.js\n   CHANGE: Draw an SVG cubic bezier from the nearest orbit point to the row's right edge with stroke 1px rgba(255,255,255,.6), stroke-dasharray 2 6, 3px end dots, and a travelling 4px orange pulse via a stroke-dashoffset animation.\n6. PROBLEM: The breadcrumb starts with a teal gradient 'SW' logo tile and ends with a '···' button; the target breadcrumb is plain mono uppercase text with no tile.\n   WHERE: Top-left of the header\n   FILE: tools/watch-assets/cockpit-view.js\n   CHANGE: Replace the tile with a mono text crumb (SWARM / THE HIVE / project) in the same letter-spacing and colour as the rest of the line, and move '···' to the end of the right-hand stats line.\n7. PROBLEM: An extra RUN STREAM block sits between the worker stream and the stack, mostly empty with one card; the target goes straight from the 2x2 stream grid to the stack.\n   WHERE: Below the worker stream\n   FILE: tools/watch-assets/cockpit-view.js\n   CHANGE: Fold the orchestrator run into the worker stream grid as a card with a teal top rule, or render it as a one-line strip styled like the loop strip so the page keeps the target's vertical rhythm.\n8. PROBLEM: The robot's bloom is weaker than the target's strong orange radial glow behind and beneath the sprite.\n   WHERE: Centre robot\n   FILE: tools/watch-assets/cc-cockpit.css\n   CHANGE: Add a ::before radial-gradient (rgba(255,120,80,.35) to transparent at 60%) sized 1.6x the robot behind it, and filter: drop-shadow(0 0 30px rgba(255,110,70,.45)) on the sprite.\n\nCOORDINATOR NOTES: column balance: split the ticket list into two columns of up to ten rows each, numbered continuously (01-20) across both, ordered as the target implies (active/next on the left, done at the end), and derive every count shown on the page (header, columns, stack, worker stream) from the same ledger list so they never disagree. The floating help button is created by cc-tour.js (Hive job): do not add your own; if it overlaps your content, leave a clear note in your summary. Remove the extra RUN STREAM block (fold its one useful line into the NOW RUNNING card).",
