+        "problem": "Session log panel has a large empty gap (about 150px) between the last log row and the terminal line + bar chart; the target's log fills its panel.",
+        "where": "Bottom-left panel, below the fold",
+        "file": "tools/watch-assets/hive-panels.js, tools/watch-assets/cc-hive.css",
+        "change": "Make the log list flex:1 with overflow:hidden and feed it the full recent ledger event stream (all events in time order, not one summary row per project per state) so it fills the available height; alternatively stack the terminal line and chart directly after the list and let the panel grid use align-items:start."
+      },
+      {
+        "problem": "Mini bar chart is sparse: a handful of tall blue bars with tiny coloured stubs, where the target shows a dense multi-colour bar field spanning the panel width.",
+        "where": "Bottom of the session log panel",
+        "file": "tools/watch-assets/hive-panels.js",
+        "change": "Render one 3px bar per bucket across the full panel width (e.g. per project x status, or per ledger time slice), normalise heights to the bucket max so no single series dominates, colour each bar by lane and clamp heights to the chart box."
+      },
+      {
+        "problem": "Middle panel composition differs from the target: the big number should be followed by a two-part coloured sentence and a one-line lane list, and the extra 'DONE PER PROJECT' grid is not in the target.",
+        "where": "ALL PROJECTS panel, below the fold",
+        "file": "tools/watch-assets/hive-panels.js, tools/watch-assets/cc-hive.css",
+        "change": "Lay out: big pink number + 'projects.' + a second phrase in lane colour (e.g. live agent count), then a mono line listing the lanes separated by middle dots, a hairline, then the WHO IS BUILDING NOW bars. Move the done-per-project values into the third panel's step chart tooltip or drop the grid."
